# =====================================================================
# Release V042 -- practice-site attribution for appointments
# =====================================================================
# All facts for real Dentally practices were resolving fk_Practice_Site to the
# sentinel (-1) -> reporting could not split by practice site. Root cause: the
# APPOINTMENT load lost its site source. Real Dentally carries site as a GUID;
# appointments as practitioner_site_id (100% filled on Tenant 100), not site_id.
# Bronze/Silver *06 REMOVED the site read ("not in Dentally API" -- wrong) and
# derived site only from the (empty) rooms path -> NULL -> sentinel.
#
# Fix (warehouse-only; NO re-pull -- Ingest_Dentally already lands practitioner_site_id
# + room_id in stage_appointments):
#   * Bronze.Appointments      + Practitioner_Site_ID VARCHAR(50); SP reads practitioner_site_id.
#   * Silver.Appointments      + Practitioner_Site_ID; room-derived Site_ID renamed -> Room_Site_ID
#                              (two genuinely different sites kept distinct: the practitioner's site
#                              vs the site of the room the appt took place in).
#   * Gold.Fact_Appointments   fk_Practice_Site now joins on a.Practitioner_Site_ID (was room Site_ID).
#
# The dimension (Dim_Practice_Sites.Site_ID VARCHAR(50)) + all fact joins were already
# GUID-safe; invoices/payments/patients/nhs_claims/referrals/contracts still read site_id
# and are structurally fine (verify post-build, no code change).
#
# DESTRUCTIVE: the two .Table.sql are DROP/CREATE -> Bronze + Silver Appointments are
# emptied and rebuilt from stage. Agreed with AIH ("happy to blow away Appointments").
# Deploy order matters (Fabric validates columns at CREATE time): TABLES before SPs.
#
# PRECONDITION: stage_appointments must expose practitioner_site_id (true after the real
# T100 ingest). If the SQL endpoint cached an older schema, recreate Stage.Appointments
# (Stage.Views.sql) first.
#
# AFTER deploy: re-run Orchestrate_Build (Bronze->Silver->Gold) for affected tenants, then
# validate: SELECT fk_Practice_Site, COUNT(*) FROM Gold.Fact_Appointments WHERE Tenant_ID=100
# GROUP BY fk_Practice_Site  -> expect the real site pk, not -1.
#
# TODO (separate): generate_data.py must emit practitioner_site_id for synthetic tenants
# (T11-14) so dev appointments also attribute; mergeSchema means mixed stage is fine (NULL
# until then). Do NOT remove the PBI Practice Site filter -- single-site practices just get a
# 1-item list.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V042__site_attribution_appointments.manifest
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY   Fabric\Bronze.Appointments.Table.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Silver.Appointments.Table.sql

DEPLOY   Fabric\Bronze.usp_Load_Appointments.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Silver.usp_Load_Appointments.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY   Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Fact_Appointments.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
